<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pausanias (general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 470 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Pausanias the regent · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agiad-dynasty">Agiad dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pausanias was a Spartan general and regent for the young king Pleistarchus. He commanded the Greek army that defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a> in 479 BCE and in 478 BCE took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>. His arrogance towards the allies led them to turn to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, which formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a>. Accused of intrigue with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, he took refuge in a temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and was starved to death there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pausanias-general.jpg" alt="Pausanias (general)" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jona Lendering · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pausanias_in_the_Capitoline_Museums,_Rome.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 478 BCE the Greek fleet under the Spartan regent <b>Pausanias</b> captured Byzantium from the Persians; his arrogance there helped drive the allies to accept Athenian leadership.</blockquote><a href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 480 BCE Leonidas I held the pass of Thermopylae with a small Greek force including 300 Spartiates until he was outflanked and killed, and in 479 BCE the regent <b>Pausanias</b> commanded the Greek army that destroyed the Persian land forces at the Battle of Plataea.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sparta">Sparta · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After the defeat of Xerxes, the Ionian and Aegean Greeks wanted to continue the war against Persia and resented the Spartan commander <b>Pausanias</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a></li><li><blockquote>The arrogance of the Spartan regent <b>Pausanias</b> at Byzantium in 478 BCE led the Ionian allies to turn to Athens, which founded the Delian League.</blockquote><a href="/state/hellenic-alliance">Hellenic Alliance</a></li><li><blockquote>In 479 BCE the allied Greek army under the Spartan <b>Pausanias</b> defeated the Persian general Mardonius on its territory, and the city was charged with tending the graves of the fallen and hosting a festival of freedom, the Eleutheria.</blockquote><a href="/state/plataea">Plataea</a></li></ul></section>
